WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:02.534
-Thank you!
Welcome, welcome, welcome!

00:00:02.534 --> 00:00:04.200
Enjoy yourself.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.634
You're here, you made it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:08.334
Thank you for watching.

00:00:08.334 --> 00:00:10.567
Well, guys, everyone
is talking about this.

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:12.834
As of tonight's taping,
Republicans still

00:00:12.834 --> 00:00:15.467
have not chosen
a speaker of the House

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.868
after Kevin McCarthy lost his
sixth vote in Congress.

00:00:18.868 --> 00:00:20.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:23.467
To be honest, it's hard to get
every Republican on board.

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:26.467
It's like getting 218 friends to
agree on where to have brunch.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.367
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.367 --> 00:00:30.067
At this point,
McCarthy's so unpopular,

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:32.434
even Southwest Airlines
feels bad for him, you know?

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:35.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:37.267
But this is interesting --
according to the Constitution,

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.200
if they don't have a speaker
by tomorrow,

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:41.701
the top contenders have
to compete in a dance-off.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:44.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.734
That's right,
McCarthy has already lost

00:00:45.734 --> 00:00:47.300
six votes to get the job.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:49.300
It's pretty humiliating,
but he's not giving up.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:50.901
He's even got
a different campaign slogan

00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.601
for each round of voting.

00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:54.033
Yeah, check this out.

00:00:54.033 --> 00:00:55.767
For the first vote,
his slogan was...

00:00:58.267 --> 00:00:59.934
For the second vote, it was...

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.167 --> 00:01:04.734
For the third vote, it was...

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:08.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:09.834
For the next vote, it was...

00:01:12.501 --> 00:01:13.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.501 --> 00:01:15.000
Then, it was...

00:01:18.167 --> 00:01:19.334
[ Laughter ]

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:20.834
Next, it's...

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.601
Then it was...

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:28.467
Then it was...

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.567
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.567 --> 00:01:35.567
Then it's...

00:01:37.834 --> 00:01:38.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:39.934
And finally, it's...

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:44.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.200
At least he's prepared.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.634
[ Applause ]

00:01:50.634 --> 00:01:53.033
That's right, lawmakers have
been staying at the Capitol

00:01:53.033 --> 00:01:54.901
around the clock to try
and secure the votes.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:57.000
And this is actual footage
of a delivery

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:59.033
that was wheeled into
McCarthy's office last night.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.601
Look at this.
Look at all this pizza.

00:02:01.601 --> 00:02:02.601
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.601 --> 00:02:04.901
Yeah, that's real.
Yeah.

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:07.300
Sadly -- Sadly,
McCarthy lost three more votes

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.000
when he took a slice
of ham and pineapple.

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:11.100
-Oh.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.067
-We don't do that.
That's right,

00:02:13.067 --> 00:02:15.567
everyone sat around eating
while George Santos claimed

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.501
that his great-grandfather
invented pizza.

00:02:17.501 --> 00:02:19.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.300
That's right.
The big news is that we still

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:22.667
don't have
a speaker of the House,

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:26.000
which means Congress can't
convene or swear in new members,

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:27.701
which means we don't have
a functioning government

00:02:27.701 --> 00:02:29.701
right now, which means...

00:02:30.634 --> 00:02:32.901
[ Dick Dale's "Misirlou" plays ]

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:42.901
♪♪

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:47.133
♪♪

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:48.934
No rules!

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:50.167
-Hi, Mr. Fallon.

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.467
Ohh!

00:02:51.467 --> 00:03:01.534
♪♪

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.667
♪♪

00:03:03.667 --> 00:03:05.033
Ohh!
-No rules!

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:06.868
-Ohh!

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:12.801
♪♪

00:03:12.801 --> 00:03:14.400
[ Music stops ]

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:16.367 --> 00:03:17.868
Some more political news, uh...

00:03:17.868 --> 00:03:22.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.934
Today, President Biden
travelled to Kentucky

00:03:24.934 --> 00:03:26.667
where he made a rare
joint appearance

00:03:26.667 --> 00:03:29.334
with Senate Minority Leader
Mitch McConnell.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.834
It was actually
a very sweet moment

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:32.734
when they fell asleep
during each other's speeches.

00:03:32.734 --> 00:03:36.067
[ Laughter ]

00:03:36.067 --> 00:03:38.767
McConnell even got to ride
in the presidential limo.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:40.200
-Ooh.
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.968
And unlike Trump,
Biden didn't have the car

00:03:41.968 --> 00:03:44.067
suddenly pull away every time
Mitch tried to get in.

00:03:44.067 --> 00:03:46.167
[ Laughter ]

00:03:46.167 --> 00:03:49.734
"Come on, dude.
It's not funny."

00:03:49.734 --> 00:03:51.467
Hey, guys, get this --
Donald Trump Jr.

00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.200
posted a video
on Facebook yesterday,

00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:55.400
and people noticed that he used
a lot of air quotes.

00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.834
Watch this.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:04:01.234
-But this is a person who was
wrapped up in that scandal.

00:04:01.234 --> 00:04:03.767
She ran a fund
that was involved in it.

00:04:03.767 --> 00:04:07.634
A "close colleague of crypto
King Sam Bankman-Fried,

00:04:07.634 --> 00:04:10.234
Ellison is now pleading guilty,

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:14.234
saying she knew
what they did was illegal."

00:04:14.234 --> 00:04:16.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.501 --> 00:04:18.267
-I'm not sure Donald Trump Jr.

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:20.634
understands
how finger quotes work.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:24.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.467 --> 00:04:26.200
At that point,
you're not doing air quotes.

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.868
You're doing a play
about two bunnies.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:31.000
You know what I'm saying?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:33.601
And this is going viral -- on a
recent United Airlines flight,

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:35.968
one of the passengers lost
a pretty important item.

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.701
This is real.
Take a look at this.

00:04:37.701 --> 00:04:40.834
-Anybody missing a cat?

00:04:40.834 --> 00:04:41.868
No?

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.133
-I think it's
from way back there.

00:04:43.133 --> 00:04:45.968
-Watch out, guys.
Anybody missing a cat?

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:52.400
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:54.167
-Then, the pilot
got on the loudspeaker like,

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:57.767
"What the hell is happening
to the airline industry?

00:04:57.767 --> 00:04:59.334
I mean,
we're dressed in suits up here.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:01.400
What is going on with people?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.934
Meanwhile, to cover it,
the airline was like,

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.133
"Tonight's in-flight
entertainment is a live showing

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:06.200
of 'Puss in Boots.'"

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.167
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.000
Guys, it's the first week
of 2023,

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.901
and with everyone making
their New Year's resolutions,

00:05:11.901 --> 00:05:14.234
all the gyms are trying
to sign up new members.

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:15.801
Check out how one of them
is going after people.

00:05:15.801 --> 00:05:16.834
It's interesting.

00:05:16.834 --> 00:05:18.367
-If you're looking
to get in shape,

00:05:18.367 --> 00:05:20.467
come on down to Planet Fitness.

00:05:20.467 --> 00:05:23.734
We've got treadmills, weights,
ellipticals, TVs,

00:05:23.734 --> 00:05:27.000
pool tables, stools,
beer on tap, jalapeño poppers,

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.200
darts, a jukebox,
and trivia night.

00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:35.133
-Yeah, not bad.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:36.667
That's a good idea.

00:05:36.667 --> 00:05:39.801
[ Applause ]

00:05:39.801 --> 00:05:42.033
That's right,
it's the start of the new year,

00:05:42.033 --> 00:05:44.100
and we're four days
into dry January,

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:46.868
which is when people stop
drinking alcohol for 31 days.

00:05:46.868 --> 00:05:49.400
Then on February 1st,
you basically hit your liver

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:51.000
with a flying elbow
off the top rope.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.534 --> 00:05:53.901
'Course, a lot of people
are still talking about

00:05:53.901 --> 00:05:55.334
their New Year's resolutions.

00:05:55.334 --> 00:05:57.868
My resolution this year
is to travel more.

00:05:57.868 --> 00:05:59.701
Quest, what's yours?

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:01.601
-Hey, I'm gonna go to the gym
more, you know?

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:04.100
My calves are gonna be
as buff as phonebooks.

00:06:04.100 --> 00:06:05.968
-Nice. What about you, Higgins?

00:06:05.968 --> 00:06:08.534
-[ Coughs ]
-I'm cutting back on smoking.

00:06:08.534 --> 00:06:10.400
Now I'm on -- [ Coughs ]
just like three packs a day.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:12.033
That's it.
-That's good. That's great.

00:06:12.033 --> 00:06:14.734
James, what about your
New Year's resolution?

00:06:14.734 --> 00:06:16.467
-[ Speaking Na'vi ]

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.734
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.000 --> 00:06:59.601
-What?

00:06:59.601 --> 00:07:01.934
-[ Speaking Na'vi ]

00:07:12.234 --> 00:07:14.267
[ Laughs ]

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:30.334
[ Laughter ]

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.200
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.334 --> 00:07:57.834
Come on.

00:07:57.834 --> 00:07:59.667
[ Rimshot ]

00:08:04.367 --> 00:08:06.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:10.767 --> 00:08:13.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.934 --> 00:08:25.534
What?

00:08:25.534 --> 00:08:26.901
[ Laughter ]

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:28.868
-Oh, my God.

00:08:28.868 --> 00:08:31.901
Okay.

00:08:31.901 --> 00:08:33.234
Alright.

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:40.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:42.868 --> 00:08:44.367
-Wow.

00:08:44.367 --> 00:08:48.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.501 --> 00:08:50.000
-Wow!

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.834
He already learned Na'vi.
That's great.

00:08:51.834 --> 00:08:54.334
-He speaks fluent Na'vi, yeah.

00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:56.267
-He's a whiz with an air fryer.

00:08:56.267 --> 00:08:59.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:59.033 --> 00:09:01.868
-Guys, I read that researchers
are working to develop

00:09:01.868 --> 00:09:03.667
a new smart device that can tell

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:06.501
whether you have COVID
or the flu.

00:09:06.501 --> 00:09:07.567
They even have
a good name for it.

00:09:07.567 --> 00:09:09.167
It's called a COVID test.

00:09:09.167 --> 00:09:10.667
[ Laughter ]

00:09:10.667 --> 00:09:12.133
Stick around!
We'll be right back

00:09:12.133 --> 00:09:14.133
with "Battle of
the Instant Songwriters"!

